description:
In repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/feature-compose.ts, report each drafting model's outcome to the grading endpoint. TWO edits in this one file. A previous attempt failed typecheck with 'TS2300: Duplicate identifier endpoint', so note carefully: DECLARE NOTHING. Introduce no const, no let, no parameter, no function. Both replacements below contain only assignments to globalThis properties and a fetch call. Copy them verbatim.

Edit A. Replace this line, which occurs exactly once:
  console.log("[fc-draft-model] selected=" + String((j as { model_selection?: { selected?: unknown } })?.model_selection?.selected ?? "unknown") + " task=feature_compose");

with exactly these three lines:
  (globalThis as Record<string, unknown>).__fcDraftModel = String((j as { model_selection?: { selected?: unknown } })?.model_selection?.selected ?? "");
  (globalThis as Record<string, unknown>).__fcDraftEndpoint = endpoint;
  console.log("[fc-draft-model] pick=" + String((globalThis as Record<string, unknown>).__fcDraftModel ?? "") + " task=feature_compose");

Edit B. Replace these two consecutive lines, which occur exactly once:
    writeFileSync(
      reportPath,

with exactly these lines:
    void fetch(String((globalThis as Record<string, unknown>).__fcDraftEndpoint ?? ""), {
      method: "POST",
      headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json", Authorization: "ApiKey " + METABOB_API_KEY },
      body: JSON.stringify({
        type: "llmArmOutcome_write",
        model: String((globalThis as Record<string, unknown>).__fcDraftModel ?? ""),
        reached: verdict === "FAVORABLE",
        task_type: "feature_compose",
      }),
    }).catch(() => {});
    writeFileSync(
      (reportPath),

The identifier endpoint already exists as a parameter of the enclosing llmCall function and must NOT be redeclared; edit A only reads it. The identifiers verdict and METABOB_API_KEY already exist in scope at edit B and must NOT be redeclared either.

The receiving endpoint already exists and is verified live: llm-resolver-vessel serves the shape llmArmOutcome_write, landed in commit fec22cbc, and an operator probe returned resolved true. Its handler forwards to recordArmOutcome, which already maintains the per-task task_alpha and task_beta posteriors. Drafting is currently the only work the selector collects no evidence about: feature_compose and patch_with_tools carry zero learned posterior while seven other task types are graded. The fetch is fire-and-forget with a catch and cannot affect any verdict.

